st i try to be data-driven in  everything that i do  but i really felt that this was a very  real  possibility and it deserved a full  investigation and it was  only in the beginning of this year uh  2021  that that started to turn i know i had  i wrote some things uh someone named  nicholson baker he had a great piece in  new york  magazine um the wall street journal did  a great job  um covering this and so this the space  was starting to  to open up then they had that really  in my mind ill-fated press event in  wuhan where it was this  independent committee and the chinese  government and they said  don't investigate lab leak investigate  the frozen food  hypothesis and then in every newspaper  around the world  the headline was the world health  organization  says don't lab leak is not is not  possible essentially and so i  immediately sent messages to my my  friends  at the world health organization and  saying look you're this is being  misreported  the world health organization hasn't  said this  and the the position of the who  must be we have to investigate all  hypotheses  and i was very pleased that three days  later so the press event was on a  tuesday that friday  tedros adenom who's the director general  he then  said in a press event that we believe  that every  hypothesis needs to be investigated  which implicitly  meant the lab leak hypothesis and then  our letter  uh came out which was just uh just last  week i mean it feels  it's been such a whirlwind since then  and that's been picked up in  newspapers all around the world so now i  feel like there  is an opening and i hope that we can  continue and the goal  in my mind isn't to prove like i don't i  don't feel like i need to  maybe if it's provable i'd love to prove  it but it's not to prove that right this  point  that it is a lab leak or isn't but we at  least need to have  the most thorough unrestricted  unpoliticized investigation into what  happened  with access to all the lab records all 